      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T00:03:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m unclear how the `UCSI_CMD_GET_PD_MESSAGE` command factors into this condition. This is setting the bit in response to `UCSI_CMD_GET_CAPABILITY`. Should that be the command we are checking for?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1394,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1394,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "85c8d9c21d921fe7c3f21ff494b36dfc97266342",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "582d44fb_e4f84ea1",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1394,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T15:35:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be the GET_VDO subcommand (0x9a)?",
      "parentUuid": "076ec802_7711fb98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1394,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1394,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "85c8d9c21d921fe7c3f21ff494b36dfc97266342",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19e555e3_db279bb5",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1394,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T15:57:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, the purpose of setting this bit is to satisfy this condition in the kernel\u0027s UCSI driver (https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/v6.6/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c;drc\u003dad44794717b5069a207ff689dec39a90c62b7567;l\u003d1205). There is another one which controls whether or not cable discovery will be attempted.\n\nIf that condition isn\u0027t met, then the driver wouldn\u0027t send GET_PD_MESSAGE, and subsequently the PPM won\u0027t send GET_VDOs. So, I think setting this bit will come before any GET_PD_MESSAGE or GET_VDO messages. And, the bit getting set here is in the UCSI_CMD_GET_CAPABILITY response.",
      "parentUuid": "582d44fb_e4f84ea1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1394,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1394,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "85c8d9c21d921fe7c3f21ff494b36dfc97266342",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ffa1e52_92158617",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1394,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T18:48:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes this should be UCSI_CMD_GET_CAPABILITY. I\u0027ll also compare `wr_buf` to make sure we\u0027re sending a UCSI command. \n\nPTAL.",
      "parentUuid": "19e555e3_db279bb5",
